  "definitions_english": {
    "greatest": "By definition, for every first point, the first point is greatest exactly when every second point ranks below the first point.\n",
    "least": "By definition, for every first point, the first point is minimum exactly when for every second point, if it is not the case that the second point is the same as the first point, then the first point precedes the second point.\n",
    "minimal": "By definition, for every first point, the first point is minimal exactly when every second point does not precede the first point.\n",
    "sim": "By definition, for every first point, for every second point, the first point matches the second point exactly when both the first point ranks below the second point and the second point ranks below the first point.\n"
  },
